{"uid":"f71cb7af7bedc415","name":"test_resolve_container_host_path_recovers_a_relocated_ancestor_mount","fullName":"tests.test_docker_sibling_e2e#test_resolve_container_host_path_recovers_a_relocated_ancestor_mount","historyId":"a71eb1679e53bcb0c27d5a6f635f5e2b","time":{"start":1791939000011,"stop":1791939005059,"duration":5048},"description":"Task 012 (requirement I.2): `scripts/resolve_container_host_path.sh`\n    must recover the REAL host path behind an in-container path even when\n    that path's own mount has no `Destination` entry of its own -- only an\n    ANCESTOR of it does. This is exactly GitHub Actions' own\n    `container:` shape (`$GITHUB_WORKSPACE` is a subdirectory of the\n    single `/__w` bind, measured directly on the retired heavy workflow run 35163222049 --\n    see that script's own header) and the reason a naive\n    `docker run -v \"$GITHUB_WORKSPACE\":...` mounted an empty directory the\n    first time this task ran it for real.\n\n    Proven against a REAL nested container, never a mock of `docker\n    inspect`: an outer sibling mounts this repo's own real host workspace\n    one level ABOVE where the script is asked to resolve from (`/relocated`,\n    not `/relocated/pyproject.toml`), then a THIRD, independently spawned\n    sibling mounts whatever host path the script printed and must find this\n    repo's own `pyproject.toml` there.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 012 (requirement I.2): <code>scripts/resolve_container_host_path.sh</code><br />\nmust recover the REAL host path behind an in-container path even when<br />\nthat path's own mount has no <code>Destination</code> entry of its own -- only an<br />\nANCESTOR of it does. This is exactly GitHub Actions' own<br />\n<code>container:</code> shape (<code>$GITHUB_WORKSPACE</code> is a subdirectory of the<br />\nsingle <code>/__w</code> bind, measured directly on the retired heavy workflow run 35163222049 --<br />\nsee that script's own header) and the reason a naive<br />\n<code>docker run -v &quot;$GITHUB_WORKSPACE&quot;:...</code> mounted an empty directory the<br />\nfirst time this task ran it for real.</p>\n<pre><code>Proven against a REAL nested container, never a mock of `docker\ninspect`: an outer sibling mounts this repo's own real host workspace\none level ABOVE where the script is asked to resolve from (`/relocated`,\nnot `/relocated/pyproject.toml`), then a THIRD, independently spawned\nsibling mounts whatever host path the script printed and must find this\nrepo's own `pyproject.toml` there.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791938419430,"stop":1791938419431,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791938419430,"stop":1791938419430,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791939000010,"stop":1791939000010,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791939000010,"stop":1791939000010,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_scrub_notifier_env_in_process","time":{"start":1791939000010,"stop":1791939000011,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCoun